-- MM2 UNIVERSAL: automatic PC + mobile controls, with bundled WindUI.
-- PC: left-click fires/stabs, E or right-click throws, Right Shift shows/hides the menu.
-- The floating MM2 bubble is mobile-only; the PC menu key consumes Right Shift.
-- Mobile: draggable MM2 icon + separate FIRE/STAB and THROW buttons.
-- Players tab: role-aware or selected-player fling attempts, with Stop/return.
-- Active input selects the layout; touch-capable PCs keep mouse/keyboard controls.
-- Replace your GitHub main.lua with this ENTIRE file. The existing loader URL stays the same.
-- An access key is required at launch; nothing else starts until a valid key is entered.
-- Device/executor compatibility needs live testing; hits remain server-authoritative.
-- Murder Mystery 2 aim assist + role/gun ESP + optional dropped-gun pickup.
-- Silent aim is ON at startup. Left-click shoots the gun or stabs with the knife.
-- E, right-button press, or the native touch throw action explicitly starts a knife throw.
-- Clicking with the knife never automatically throws, regardless of target distance.
-- Aimed shots/throws are skipped if no unobstructed body target is available.
-- Gun targets the known murderer in 3D; knife throws can acquire clear offscreen targets.
-- Clear-target protection skips unaimed assisted throws; clicked stab assist selects a nearby clear opponent.
-- Camera and cursor are never moved. F6 toggles silent aim and restores native handlers.
-- Magic Bullet (F7) separately toggles immediate gun redirection to the known murderer.
-- Magic Bullet OFF restores the native gun controller; knife assist has its own toggle.
-- Auto pickup uses simulated touch only; server distance checks may reject it.
-- Repair character respawns an avatar affected by an older root-swap version.
-- Knife speed follows replicated ThrowingKnife attributes (MM2 default: 96).
-- Auto knife dodge jumps low incoming paths or briefly sidesteps using normal movement; menu toggle stops it.
-- Dodge checks incoming direction, timing, walls, ceilings, and floor support; survival is not guaranteed.
-- Jump prediction includes vertical velocity, gravity, and the landing surface.
-- Partial cover uses exposed torso/head/limb points; fully blocked shots are skipped.
-- Invisible solid map objects block the shot check; only unconfirmed transparent non-solid helpers are skipped.
-- Recent replicated positions cross-check reported velocity after stops/turns.
-- Gun motion history is sampled at up to 50 Hz; consistent steering, acceleration, and braking use bounded prediction.
-- Abrupt reversals/zigzags discard the curved model and use fresh velocity; no future input can be guaranteed.
-- Stable grounded targets use zero lead and additional exposed-edge samples when their body center is blocked.
-- Stationary and close approaching targets can use their existing queryable root as a stable central gun aim point.
-- Existing named body parts are ranked by projected area and clearance around the shot.
-- Wider interior samples find exposed edges in narrow spaces; character hitboxes are unchanged.
-- Nearby threat warning shows camera-relative direction, distance, and closing movement.
-- Fresh horizontal velocity changes take priority over older position samples after turns.
-- A small gun aim marker shows the selected body point without moving the cursor.
-- Gun motion prediction checks nearby collision walls and allows bounded wall sliding.
-- Aim rays are checked against visible body geometry, including extra corner samples.
-- Knife interception is refined for the exact selected body offset at release.
-- Optional stab sweep reports nearby blade overlaps during a clicked stab only.
-- Fresh jump/apex/landing velocity changes override older vertical samples.
-- Observed airborne velocity is corrected from the sample midpoint to the latest instant.
-- Invisible opponents use their existing named body geometry; ESP draws hidden-part boxes.
-- Gun samples are ranked across early/nominal/late motion hypotheses without delaying a click.
-- Gun acquisition follows the known murderer in 3D even outside the camera view.
-- Depth and XZ samples cover high/low viewing angles; walls still block shots.
-- Optional R15 poses use the existing Animator; no head deletion or avatar resizing.
-- Mage locomotion is ON by default: idle, walk, run, jump, fall, climb, and swim.
-- ANIMS / F9 toggles Mage; original animation IDs are restored on OFF or unload.
-- Mage retries late character setup and reapplies if the game replaces/resets Animate.
-- Attacking exits the pose and restores normal body/weapon geometry before firing or stabbing.
-- Coin/gun touch pickup is experimental; only real CoinCollected events are counted.
-- Floating/bend poses do not remove the head. Other-client visibility is not independently verified.
-- Knife candidates are ranked cheaply first; expensive prediction is evaluated only where it can change the selection.
-- Re-running replaces the previous instance; Insert hides/shows the panel without toggling native shift lock.
-- Fix camera / F10 clears stale native input and mouse lock; saved sensitivity and zoom are preserved.
-- The camera guard clears unselected mouse locks and preserves actual shift lock, first person, and camera rotation.
